# Isotropic sensitivity kernels for splitting function data based on cst_mdcplmrho_all programmes
# Kernels are calculated by putting a unit input into cst_mdcplmrho_kernels-all_vs-vp-rho-topo-all 
# and recording the recovered predicted value
# This includes OC and IC structure (unlike Restelli et al where sensitivity in the core was 0)

# Kernels values are given in separate files for each mode and physical parameter:
# kern_${mode}_${parameter}_PREM-layers-all_PREM-iso.kern
# These are organised in the following way:

s layer kern_val
s layer kern_val
s layer kern_val
s layer kern_val

with:
- s:         the degree of the spherical harmonic degree (from 0 to max 20)
- layer:     the PREM layer number that the value corresponds to
- kern_val:  the value of the sensitivity kernel in this depth layer

# For PREM, the layers are numbered 1 to 222 with some layers indicating discontinuities
# The intervals (in radius) of the layers are indicated in the files
# PREM_all-layers_radius and PREM_all-layers_radius_no-disc

# The kernel values have been tested (amplitude and pattern) against the modeplotaat code.
# This matches for vs, vp, rho at present, needs some checking still for topo. 



